{
    "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/martinring/tmlanguage/master/tmlanguage.json",
    "name": "Craft",
    "scopeName": "source.craft",
    "fileTypes": [".craft"],
    "patterns": [
        { "include": "#comment" },
        { "include": "#string" },
        { "include": "#actor-declaration" },
        { "include": "#domain-declaration" },
        { "include": "#service-declaration" },
        { "include": "#use-case-declaration" },
        { "include": "#block-keywords" },
        { "include": "#flow-keyword" },
        { "include": "#relationship-edge" },
        { "include": "#event-ref" },
        { "include": "#action-verbs" },
        { "include": "#relationship-verbs" },
        { "include": "#node-slug" },
        { "include": "#connector-keywords" },
        { "include": "#actor-types" },
        { "include": "#property-keywords" },
        { "include": "#section-keywords" },
        { "include": "#entity-name" },
        { "include": "#number" },
        { "include": "#boolean" },
        { "include": "#punctuation" }
    ],
    "repository": {
        "comment": {
            "comment": "A comment only begins where the lexer says it does: at line start, or immediately after whitespace (internal/lexer/lexer.go, precededByWS). Without that guard a slash inside flexible prose (craft >= 2.9.0) is mis-scoped — `asks Y for http://api` would colour the rest of the line as a comment.",
            "patterns": [
                {
                    "name": "comment.line.double-slash",
                    "match": "(?:^|(?<=[ \\t]))//.*$"
                },
                {
                    "name": "comment.block",
                    "begin": "(?:^|(?<=[ \\t]))/\\*",
                    "end": "\\*/"
                }
            ]
        },
        "string": {
            "name": "string.quoted.double",
            "begin": "\"",
            "end": "\"",
            "patterns": [
                {
                    "name": "constant.character.escape",
                    "match": "\\\\."
                }
            ]
        },
        "actor-declaration": {
            "match": "^\\s*(actor)\\s+(user|system|service)\\s+([A-Z][A-Za-z0-9_]*)",
            "captures": {
                "1": { "name": "storage.type" },
                "2": { "name": "support.type" },
                "3": { "name": "entity.name.type" }
            }
        },
        "domain-declaration": {
            "match": "^\\s*(domain)\\s+([A-Z][A-Za-z0-9_]*)",
            "captures": {
                "1": { "name": "storage.type" },
                "2": { "name": "entity.name.type" }
            }
        },
        "service-declaration": {
            "match": "^\\s*(service)\\s+([A-Z][A-Za-z0-9_]*)",
            "captures": {
                "1": { "name": "storage.type" },
                "2": { "name": "entity.name.type" }
            }
        },
        "use-case-declaration": {
            "match": "^\\s*(use_case)\\s+(\"[^\"]*\")",
            "captures": {
                "1": { "name": "storage.type" },
                "2": { "name": "string.quoted.double" }
            }
        },
        "block-keywords": {
            "match": "\\b(services|domains|actors|arch|exposure|tags|context_map|glossary)\\b",
            "captures": {
                "1": { "name": "keyword.other" }
            }
        },
        "flow-keyword": {
            "match": "^\\s*(when)\\b",
            "captures": {
                "1": { "name": "keyword.control" }
            }
        },
        "action-verbs": {
            "match": "\\b(asks|notifies|listens|returns|marks)\\b",
            "captures": {
                "1": { "name": "entity.name.function" }
            }
        },
        "event-ref": {
            "comment": "Typed event ref (craft >= 2.9.0): `notifies order.OrderCreated`, `when Payment listens order.OrderCreated`. Qualifier and event name get distinct scopes; an unqualified `notifies OrderCreated` colours just the name. The negative lookahead skips slug-shaped refs (`notifies bc:re/x`) so #node-slug handles those rather than this rule swallowing the kind word. The legacy quoted form never reaches here: #string is earlier in the pattern list. Segment charset mirrors the lexer's identifier rule (letters, digits, _, -, . — internal/lexer/lexer.go isIdentChar).",
            "match": "\\b(notifies|listens)[ \\t]+(?![A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_-]*:)(?:([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_-]*(?:\\.[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_-]*)*)(\\.))?([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_-]*)",
            "captures": {
                "1": { "name": "entity.name.function" },
                "2": { "name": "entity.name.namespace" },
                "3": { "name": "punctuation.accessor" },
                "4": { "name": "support.class" }
            }
        },
        "relationship-edge": {
            "comment": "A whole context_map or glossary edge line, so bare endpoints get coloured too: `re/billing customer_supplier re/vas`, `Wallet/balance same_as WalletItemPurchase/balance`, `Wallet open_host_service WalletItemPurchase`. The last '/'-segment is the name (the term, for glossary), the rest is its namespace. Each endpoint may carry a kind prefix (`bc:re/x customer_supplier re/y`), so mixed lines colour symmetrically instead of half-falling-through to #node-slug.",
            "match": "^[ \\t]*(?:(domain|bc|term|service)(:))?((?:[A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*/)*)([A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*)[ \\t]+(customer_supplier|conformist|anticorruption_layer|open_host_service|published_language|partnership|shared_kernel|separate_ways|same_as|contrasts|distinct_from)[ \\t]+(?:(domain|bc|term|service)(:))?((?:[A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*/)*)([A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*)",
            "captures": {
                "1": { "name": "storage.type" },
                "2": { "name": "punctuation.separator" },
                "3": { "name": "entity.name.namespace" },
                "4": { "name": "support.class" },
                "5": { "name": "entity.name.function" },
                "6": { "name": "storage.type" },
                "7": { "name": "punctuation.separator" },
                "8": { "name": "entity.name.namespace" },
                "9": { "name": "support.class" }
            }
        },
        "relationship-verbs": {
            "comment": "context_map DDD patterns (craft >= 2.12.0) and glossary relation verbs (craft >= 2.13.0). Mirrors edgeKeywords in internal/syntax/parser.go plus the glossary verb set; keep in sync when either gains a verb.",
            "match": "\\b(customer_supplier|conformist|anticorruption_layer|open_host_service|published_language|partnership|shared_kernel|separate_ways|same_as|contrasts|distinct_from)\\b",
            "captures": {
                "1": { "name": "entity.name.function" }
            }
        },
        "node-slug": {
            "comment": "Node slug (craft >= 2.9.0): [kind:][namespace/]name — bc:re/subscriptions, term:billing/dunning, domain:re/renewal, service:subscriptions-api. Kind set mirrors isSlugKind in internal/syntax/parser.go. The colon must be adjacent to the kind word (the parser requires adjacency too), which keeps `contexts: A, B` and other `key: value` fields out of this rule; `domains:` cannot match either, since \\b(domain) fails against the trailing 's'.",
            "match": "\\b(domain|bc|term|service)(:)((?:[A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*/)*)([A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*)",
            "captures": {
                "1": { "name": "storage.type" },
                "2": { "name": "punctuation.separator" },
                "3": { "name": "entity.name.namespace" },
                "4": { "name": "support.class" }
            }
        },
        "connector-keywords": {
            "match": "\\b(to|through)\\b",
            "captures": {
                "1": { "name": "keyword.operator" }
            }
        },
        "actor-types": {
            "match": "\\b(user|system|service)\\b",
            "captures": {
                "1": { "name": "support.type" }
            }
        },
        "property-keywords": {
            "comment": "Service/exposure fields. catalog_ref: and repo: are the service anchors (craft >= 2.9.0; catalog_ref: replaced opslevel: in 2.15.0). Field set mirrors the switch in parseServiceBlock, internal/syntax/parser.go.",
            "match": "\\b(contexts|language|data-stores|deployment|catalog_ref|repo|to|through)\\s*:",
            "captures": {
                "1": { "name": "keyword.other" }
            }
        },
        "section-keywords": {
            "match": "\\b(presentation|gateway)\\s*:",
            "captures": {
                "1": { "name": "keyword.other" }
            }
        },
        "entity-name": {
            "name": "entity.name.type",
            "match": "\\b[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9_]*\\b"
        },
        "number": {
            "name": "constant.numeric",
            "match": "\\b[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?(%)?\\b"
        },
        "boolean": {
            "name": "constant.language",
            "match": "\\b(true|false)\\b"
        },
        "punctuation": {
            "patterns": [
                {
                    "name": "punctuation.definition.block",
                    "match": "[{}]"
                },
                {
                    "name": "punctuation.separator",
                    "match": ","
                },
                {
                    "name": "punctuation.separator",
                    "match": ":"
                },
                {
                    "name": "punctuation.operator",
                    "match": "->"
                },
                {
                    "name": "punctuation.operator",
                    "match": ">"
                },
                {
                    "name": "punctuation.bracket",
                    "match": "[()]"
                }
            ]
        }
    }
}
